Body:
> I'm seeing what I think is a manifestation of this bug with Qwen3.5-35B-A3B and llama.cpp. The following error appears in the llama.cpp logs.
> 
> ```
> operator(): got exception: {"error":{"code":500,"message":"\n------------\nWhile executing CallExpression at line 85, column 32 in source:\n...first %}↵            {{- raise_except
> ion('System message must be at the beginnin...\n                                           ^\nError: Jinja Exception: System message must be at the beginning.","type":"server_error"}}
> ```

I experienced the same issue today with Qwen3.5-27B-Q5_K_M.gguf in llama.cpp... it worked on one PC but not on another... the difference was a plugin that was injecting:
// "experimental.chat.system.transform": async (_input, output) => {
//   output.system.push(MEMORY_INSTRUCTIONS)
// },
This plugin was adding system messages to the conversation, which caused the same error with models that don't support the system role beyond the first message.
Once I removed it, everything worked perfectly! 
So the issue seems to be related to plugins or configurations that inject additional system messages into the conversation. Models like Ministral 3 and Qwen3.5 expect only a single system message at the start (if any), and multiple system messages throughout the conversation break them.
